# Patch files are byte-sensitive: a unified diff's context lines (including
# blank ones) must keep their exact leading whitespace and the file its trailing
# newline. Tell git never to do EOL/whitespace normalisation on them, so they
# can't be silently corrupted on checkout across platforms.
#
# NOTE: this does NOT stop an editor from trimming trailing whitespace on save —
# if you open a *.patch in an editor, disable "trim trailing whitespace" for it,
# or you'll strip the leading space off blank context lines and break the patch.
*.patch -text -whitespace
